# Recompile the C library with the tcc that has just been built -- the PE32
# counterpart of libs.kaem beside this, differing in two ways: how crt1
# gets into ${out}/lib, and no `cd`.
#
# crt1 is not recompiled here. mes-libc's own crt1 is not C at all on this
# side -- lib/windows/x86-mes-mescc/crt1.M1, hand-assembled the same way
# every round's argv/envp plumbing on this platform is -- so there is no
# crt1_c to hand tcc, and every round after the first would be recompiling
# the exact same instructions from the exact same source for no reason: it
# is copied once, the way it is copied into mes-libc's own lib/ directory
# in the first place.
#
# crti and crtn are absent outright, not merely uncompiled. Both exist on
# the ELF side to bracket .init and .fini -- and PE's own loader does not
# implement a section relocation-and-run mechanism that would give them
# anything to run against, so lib/bootstrap/mes/libc.nix's gnuSource does
# not carry them for this kernel and nothing here should expect to find
# them either.
#
# No `cd ${TMPDIR}`: every other kaem script this side of the bootstrap
# names its working paths explicitly rather than changing into one, and
# that is deliberate here too, not just carried over -- kaem's cd is a
# native chdir(), and nothing else on this side has proven that call
# behaves the way this build would need under the exec-wrapper this
# chain builds through. Every intermediate .o below is written straight
# into ${out}/lib and read back from there, so there is no cwd to be
# wrong about.

${bin_mkdir} -p ${out}/lib

${bin_cp} ${crt1_o} ${out}/lib/crt1.o

# libtcc1 is the COMPILER's runtime, not the C library's: the helpers tcc
# emits calls to for arithmetic the instruction set does not do in one go.
# It comes from tinycc's own lib/, beside the compiler being built -- not
# from the Mes C library, which ships a file of the same name meaning
# something else.  Taking the wrong one leaves the helpers subtly wrong: casts
# from floating point to integer quietly produce zero.
${tcc} -std=c11 -I ${incConfig} -I ${incMes} -I ${incMesArch} -D TCC_TARGET_${tccTarget}=1 ${libtccOpt1} ${libtccOpt2} ${libtccOpt3} -c -o ${out}/lib/libtcc1.o ${libtcc1_c}
${tcc} -std=c11 -I ${incConfig} -I ${incMes} -I ${incMesArch} -D TCC_TARGET_${tccTarget}=1 ${libtccOpt1} ${libtccOpt2} ${libtccOpt3} -c -o ${out}/lib/va_list.o ${valist_c}
${tcc} -ar ${out}/lib/libtcc1.a ${out}/lib/libtcc1.o ${out}/lib/va_list.o

${tcc} -std=c11 -I ${incConfig} -I ${incMes} -I ${incMesArch} -c -o ${out}/lib/libc.o ${libc_c}
${tcc} -ar ${out}/lib/libc.a ${out}/lib/libc.o

${tcc} -std=c11 -I ${incConfig} -I ${incMes} -I ${incMesArch} -c -o ${out}/lib/libgetopt.o ${getopt_c}
${tcc} -ar ${out}/lib/libgetopt.a ${out}/lib/libgetopt.o
